<title>USA: Alaska Gov. says oil find good for state economy.</title>
<headline>Alaska Gov. says oil find good for state economy.</headline>
<dateline>ANCHORAGE, Alaska 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alaska Governor Tony Knowles on Thursday said the discovery of Sourdough oil prospect, with a potential 100-million barrel reserve, is good news for the state's economy.</p>
<p>Earlier, BP Exploration Alaska Inc, a division of British Petroleum Co. and Chevron USA announced the find, located 50 miles east of the huge Prudhoe oil field on Alaska's North Slope.</p>
<p>&quot;The significant oil discovery at Sourdough is more good news for Alaska's oil patch and for Alaska's economy,&quot; Knowles said in statement.</p>
<p>BP said they plan to explore more to determine the field's size.</p>
